msgstr "对你创建的每个设备执行此操作。每个正常工作的端口，其 RX 指示灯__应该__都会闪烁。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:987
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Support for Cheap Multi-UART Cards"
msgstr "对廉价多 UART 卡的支持"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:990
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Contributed by Helge Oldach_ mailto:hmo@sep.hamburg.com[hmo@sep.hamburg."
"com], September 1999"
msgstr "__由 Helge Oldach 贡献__ mailto:hmo@sep.hamburg.com[hmo@sep.hamburg.com]，1999 年 9 月"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:992
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ever wondered about FreeBSD support for your 20$ multi-I/O card with two (or "
"more) COM ports, sharing IRQs? Here is how:"
msgstr "你是否想过 FreeBSD 如何支持那种售价 20$、带有两个（或更多）COM 端口且共享 IRQ 的多 I/O 卡？方法如下："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:996
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Usually the only option to support these kind of boards is to use a distinct "
"IRQ for each port.  For example, if your CPU board has an on-board [."
"filename]#COM1# port (aka [.filename]#sio0#-I/O address 0x3F8 and IRQ 4) and "
"you have an extension board with two UARTs, you will commonly need to "
"configure them as [.filename]#COM2# (aka [.filename]#sio1#-I/O address 0x2F8 "
"and IRQ 3), and the third port (aka [.filename]#sio2#) as I/O 0x3E8 and IRQ "
"5.  Obviously this is a waste of IRQ resources, as it should be basically "
"possible to run both extension board ports using a single IRQ with the "
"`COM_MULTIPORT` configuration described in the previous sections."
msgstr "通常，支持这类板卡的唯一办法是为每个端口使用不同的 IRQ。例如，如果你的 CPU 板上有一个板载 [.filename]#COM1# 端口（又称 [.filename]#sio0#，I/O 地址为 0x3F8，IRQ 为 4），并且你有一块带有两个 UART 的扩展板，通常需要将其中一个配置为 [.filename]#COM2#（又称 [.filename]#sio1#，I/O 地址为 0x2F8，IRQ 为 3），第三个端口（又称 [.filename]#sio2#）则配置为 I/O 0x3E8、IRQ 5。显然，这会浪费 IRQ 资源，因为原则上可以使用前文所述的 `COM_MULTIPORT` 配置，让扩展板上的两个端口共用一个 IRQ。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:998
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Such cheap I/O boards commonly have a 4 by 3 jumper matrix for the COM "
"ports, similar to the following:"
msgstr "这类廉价 I/O 板通常有一个用于 COM 端口的 4×3 跳线矩阵，类似于下面这样："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1007
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"            o  o  o  *\n"
"Port A               |\n"
"            o  *  o  *\n"
"Port B         |\n"
"            o  *  o  o\n"
"IRQ         2  3  4  5\n"
msgstr "            o  o  o  *\nPort A               |\n            o  *  o  *\nPort B         |\n            o  *  o  o\nIRQ         2  3  4  5\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1011
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Shown here is port A wired for IRQ 5 and port B wired for IRQ 3.  The IRQ "
"columns on your specific board may vary-other boards may supply jumpers for "
"IRQs 3, 4, 5, and 7 instead."
msgstr "这里显示的是端口 A 接到 IRQ 5，端口 B 接到 IRQ 3。你的具体板卡上的 IRQ 列可能有所不同——其他板卡可能提供 IRQ 3、4、5 和 7 的跳线。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1015
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"One could conclude that wiring both ports for IRQ 3 using a handcrafted wire-"
"made jumper covering all three connection points in the IRQ 3 column would "
"solve the issue, but no.  You cannot duplicate IRQ 3 because the output "
"drivers of each UART are wired in a \"totem pole\" fashion, so if one of the "
"UARTs drives IRQ 3, the output signal will not be what you would expect.  "
"Depending on the implementation of the extension board or your motherboard, "
"the IRQ 3 line will continuously stay up, or always stay low."
msgstr "你可能会认为，用一根自制导线制作的跳线覆盖 IRQ 3 列的全部三个连接点，让两个端口都接到 IRQ 3，就能解决这个问题；事实并非如此。你不能重复使用 IRQ 3，因为每个 UART 的输出驱动器采用“图腾柱”方式连接，因此如果其中一个 UART 驱动 IRQ 3，输出信号就不会符合预期。根据扩展板或主板的实现方式，IRQ 3 线路可能会一直保持高电平，也可能始终保持低电平。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1019
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You need to decouple the IRQ drivers for the two UARTs, so that the IRQ line "
"of the board only goes up if (and only if) one of the UARTs asserts an IRQ, "
"and stays low otherwise.  The solution was proposed by Joerg Wunsch mailto:"
"j@ida.interface-business.de[j@ida.interface-business.de]: To solder up a "
"wired-or consisting of two diodes (Germanium or Schottky-types strongly "
"preferred) and a 1 kOhm resistor.  Here is the schematic, starting from the "
"4 by 3 jumper field above:"
msgstr "你需要将两个 UART 的 IRQ 驱动器隔离，使板卡的 IRQ 线路仅在（且仅在）其中一个 UART 触发 IRQ 时变为高电平，否则保持低电平。Joerg Wunsch mailto:j@ida.interface-business.de[j@ida.interface-business.de] 提出的解决方案是：用两个二极管（强烈建议使用锗二极管或肖特基二极管）和一个 1 kOhm 电阻焊接成一个线或电路。以下是从上面的 4×3 跳线区域开始绘制的电路图："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1033
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"                          Diode\n"
"                +---------->|-------+\n"
"               /                    |\n"
"            o  *  o  o              |     1 kOhm\n"
"Port A                              +----|######|-------+\n"
"            o  *  o  o              |                   |\n"
"Port B          `-------------------+                 ==+==\n"
"            o  *  o  o              |                 Ground\n"
"                \\                   |\n"
"                 +--------->|-------+\n"
"IRQ         2  3  4  5    Diode\n"
msgstr "                          Diode\n                +---------->|-------+\n               /                    |\n            o  *  o  o              |     1 kOhm\nPort A                              +----|######|-------+\n            o  *  o  o              |                   |\nPort B          `-------------------+                 ==+==\n            o  *  o  o              |                 Ground\n                \\                   |\n                 +--------->|-------+\nIRQ         2  3  4  5    Diode\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1037
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The cathodes of the diodes are connected to a common point, together with a "
"1 kOhm pull-down resistor.  It is essential to connect the resistor to "
"ground to avoid floating of the IRQ line on the bus."
msgstr "二极管的阴极连接到同一个点，并与一个 1 kOhm 下拉电阻相连。必须将电阻接地，以避免总线上的 IRQ 线路悬空。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1040
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now we are ready to configure a kernel.  Staying with this example, we would "
"configure:"
msgstr "现在可以配置内核了。沿用此示例，我们将这样配置："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1049
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# standard on-board COM1 port\n"
"device          sio0    at isa? port \"IO_COM1\" flags 0x10\n"
"# patched-up multi-I/O extension board\n"
"options         COM_MULTIPORT\n"
"device          sio1    at isa? port \"IO_COM2\" flags 0x205\n"
"device          sio2    at isa? port \"IO_COM3\" flags 0x205 irq 3\n"
msgstr "# standard on-board COM1 port\ndevice          sio0    at isa? port \"IO_COM1\" flags 0x10\n# patched-up multi-I/O extension board\noptions         COM_MULTIPORT\ndevice          sio1    at isa? port \"IO_COM2\" flags 0x205\ndevice          sio2    at isa? port \"IO_COM3\" flags 0x205 irq 3\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1054
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Note that the `flags` setting for [.filename]#sio1# and [.filename]#sio2# is "
"truly essential; refer to man:sio[4] for details.  (Generally, the `2` in "
"the \"flags\" attribute refers to [.filename]#sio#`2` which holds the IRQ, "
"and you surely want a `5` low nibble.)  With kernel verbose mode turned on "
"this should yield something similar to this:"
msgstr "请注意，sio1 和 sio2 的 `flags` 设置至关重要；详情请参阅 man:sio[4]。（通常，“flags”属性中的 `2` 指的是保存 IRQ 的 [.filename]#sio#`2`，而低位半字节肯定应为 `5`。）启用内核详细模式后，应该会得到类似以下的输出："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1066
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"sio0: irq maps: 0x1 0x11 0x1 0x1\n"
"sio0 at 0x3f8-0x3ff irq 4 flags 0x10 on isa\n"
"sio0: type 16550A\n"
"sio1: irq maps: 0x1 0x9 0x1 0x1\n"
"sio1 at 0x2f8-0x2ff flags 0x205 on isa\n"
"sio1: type 16550A (multiport)\n"
"sio2: irq maps: 0x1 0x9 0x1 0x1\n"
"sio2 at 0x3e8-0x3ef irq 3 flags 0x205 on isa\n"
"sio2: type 16550A (multiport master)\n"
msgstr "sio0: irq maps: 0x1 0x11 0x1 0x1\nsio0 at 0x3f8-0x3ff irq 4 flags 0x10 on isa\nsio0: type 16550A\nsio1: irq maps: 0x1 0x9 0x1 0x1\nsio1 at 0x2f8-0x2ff flags 0x205 on isa\nsio1: type 16550A (multiport)\nsio2: irq maps: 0x1 0x9 0x1 0x1\nsio2 at 0x3e8-0x3ef irq 3 flags 0x205 on isa\nsio2: type 16550A (multiport master)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/serial-uart/_index.adoc:1071
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Though [.filename]#/sys/i386/isa/sio.c# is somewhat cryptic with its use of "
"the \"irq maps\" array above, the basic idea is that you observe `0x1` in "
"the first, third, and fourth place.  This means that the corresponding IRQ "
"was set upon output and cleared after, which is just what we would expect.  "
"If your kernel does not display this behavior, most likely there is "
"something wrong with your wiring."
msgstr "虽然 [.filename]#/sys/i386/isa/sio.c# 中上述“irq maps”数组的用法有些晦涩，但基本思路是观察第一个、第三个和第四个位置上的 `0x1`。这表示相应的 IRQ 在输出时被置位，之后被清除，这正是预期的行为。如果内核没有显示这种行为，最可能的原因是接线有问题。"

